<p><a href="https://philosophy.unc.edu/people/thomas-e-hill/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Thomas E. Hill, Jr.</a>, professor emeritus of philosophy at the University of North Carolina, Chapel Hill, has died.<span id="more-57901"></span></p>
<p><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class=" wp-image-57903 aligncenter" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/hill-thomas-jr-photo.jpg" alt="" width="449" height="387" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/hill-thomas-jr-photo.jpg 720w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/hill-thomas-jr-photo-300x258.jpg 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/hill-thomas-jr-photo-400x344.jpg 400w" sizes="(max-width: 449px) 100vw, 449px" /></p>
<p>Professor Hill was well-known for his work in ethics, the history of ethics, and political philosophy, and especially for his scholarship on Kantian moral and political philosophy. He is the author of <em>Beyond Duty: Kantian Ideals of Respect, Beneficence, and Appreciation</em> (2022), <em>Virtue, Rules, and Justice: Kantian Aspirations</em> (2012), <em>Human Welfare and Moral Worth: Kantian Perspectives</em> (2002), <em>Respect, Pluralism and Justice: Kantian Perspectives</em> (2000), <em>Dignity and Practical Reason in Kant’s Moral Theory</em> (1992), <em>Autonomy and Self-Respect</em> (1991), and <em>The Concept of Meaning </em>(1971), among other works. You can learn more about his writings <a href="https://philpeople.org/profiles/thomas-hill-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a> and <a href="https://philosophy.unc.edu/people/thomas-e-hill/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>.</p>
<p>Professor Hill joined the Department of Philosophy at UNC Chapel Hill in 1984. From 1968 to 1984 he taught at the University of California, Los Angeles. Prior to that, he held positions at Pomona College and Johns Hopkins University.</p>
<p>He died this week.</p><p>The post <a href="https://dailynous.com/2026/07/22/thomas-e-hill-jr-1937-2026/">Thomas E. Hill, Jr. (1937-2026)</a> first appeared on <a href="https://dailynous.com">Daily Nous</a>.</p>